# API Contracts

- Treat OpenAPI/Swagger as the source of truth for HTTP contracts when available.
- Frontend models mirror API DTOs, not database entities.
- Standardize error payloads (problem details / consistent envelope) and handle them in one HTTP interceptor path.
- Standardize list APIs: pagination, filtering, sorting query shapes.
- Never hard-code absolute API base URLs inside features; use environment/config providers.
- Auth tokens and credentials stay in `core` HTTP interceptors, not feature services.
- Prefer typed HttpClient calls; avoid `any` for request/response bodies.
- Breaking API changes require updating Angular consumers in the same change set when feasible.

## Documentation comments

Document contract intent so frontend and backend stay aligned without reading implementation.

| Scope | Required | Format |
|-------|----------|--------|
| API request/response DTO (C#) | Yes | XML `<summary>` on the type; flows into OpenAPI |
| Controller action / minimal API handler | Yes | XML `<summary>` + HTTP metadata attributes |
| Angular model mirroring a DTO | Yes | JSDoc `/** ... */` on the type or interface |
| Feature service / HTTP client method | Yes | JSDoc describing endpoint purpose and error cases |
| Interceptor / guard | Yes | Brief comment on when it runs and what it enforces |

Rules:

- Describe **contract meaning** (what the payload represents, auth requirement, typical errors) — not field-by-field repetition when names are clear.
- When a DTO or model name is ambiguous, note which API endpoint or use case it belongs to.
- Error handling paths (401, 403, 409) should be documented where the client consumes them (service or interceptor), not only on the server.
- Keep comments in English; match the language of existing files in the same folder.

```csharp
/// <summary>Payload for rotating refresh tokens.</summary>
public sealed record RefreshTokensRequest { ... }

/// <summary>Lists users. Requires the users.read permission.</summary>
[HttpGet("users")]
public async Task<IActionResult> Users(...) { }
```

```typescript
/** Mirrors AuthResponse from POST /api/identity/login. */
export interface AuthResponse { ... }

/** Calls POST /api/identity/refresh; maps 401 to session-expired handling. */
loginRefresh(refreshToken: string) { ... }
```
